  "abstract": "<jats:p>We present two new and efficient algorithms for computing all-pairs shortest paths.  The algorithms operate on directed graphs with real (possibly negative) weights.  They make use of directed path consistency along a vertex ordering d. Both algorithms run in O(n^2 w_d) time, where w_d is the graph width induced by this vertex ordering.  For graphs of constant treewidth, this yields O(n^2) time, which is optimal.  On chordal graphs, the algorithms run in O(nm) time. In addition, we present a variant that exploits graph separators to arrive at a run time of  O(n w_d^2 + n^2 s_d) on general graphs, where s_d </jats:p>",
